<item><title>South Africa&apos;s unemployment rate rises to 33.7%</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/south-africa-s-unemployment-rate-rises-to-33-7-9f5aa5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/south-africa-s-unemployment-rate-rises-to-33-7-9f5aa5/</guid><category>South Africa</category><description>Graduates still have a better chance of finding work, with an 11.9% unemployment rate in the third quarter of 2026.</description><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:32:33 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" length="36666" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Saftu rejects 3.5% salary hike for public officials</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/saftu-rejects-3-5-salary-hike-for-public-officials-bb87c8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/saftu-rejects-3-5-salary-hike-for-public-officials-bb87c8/</guid><category>South Africa</category><description>The union calls the increase indefensible amid millions struggling with unemployment and poverty.</description><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:02:31 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/saftu-rejects-3-5-salary-hike-for-public-officials-bb87c8/share.jpg" length="40686" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/saftu-rejects-3-5-salary-hike-for-public-officials-bb87c8/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Johannesburg and Cape Town set fines for parties that leave election posters up</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/johannesburg-and-cape-town-set-fines-for-parties-that-leave-7299ad/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/johannesburg-and-cape-town-set-fines-for-parties-that-leave-7299ad/</guid><category>South Africa</category><description>Cape Town will remove leftover posters by November 18 and bill parties R123.48 each, excluding VAT, while Johannesburg issues R500 per poster after a warning.</description><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:33:44 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" length="36666" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>TNPA starts US$22.5M road upgrade at Richards Bay</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/tnpa-starts-us-22-5m-road-upgrade-at-richards-bay-8bca87/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/tnpa-starts-us-22-5m-road-upgrade-at-richards-bay-8bca87/</guid><category>South Africa</category><description>The 18-month programme on Urania, Newark and Ventura Roads will strengthen pavements, widen lanes and improve drainage at the port.</description><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:19:09 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" length="36666" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
